														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4840348">
									

<p>This is a fairly decent start. You've got a heightening sense of tension, ways to speed things along without getting crazy with the timer.</p>
<p>1) Show at least two or three scientists getting weapons. If you really want to be fancy, show one getting to a weapons locker before getting killed, one getting a weapon before being killed, and the third shooting but missing before he's killed.</p>
<p>2) The scream in his ear should increase in volume with each death. It should help your tension just a little more and add to the end.</p>
<p>3) Also, you need to have the &quot;There can be only ten&quot; come out somehow at least three ways before he gets it. Yeahyeah, I know I'm giving you lots of patterns to play with and I'm probably going over somehow. However, that's because patterns have strength, and I figure that hearing it just once just makes it a random message.Backing with a pattern makes it hard to ignore.</p>
<p>But great start!</p>
<p>Otherwise, great start!</p>

