					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jamaisj" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6846344); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6846344&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607500034" alt="JamaisJ" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6846344)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jamaisj" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6846344); return false;" >JamaisJ</a></span> <span class="odate time_1607495056 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">09 Dec 2020 06:24</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13896959/harrowing-haberdashery">Harrowing Haberdashery</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4840333">
									

<p>1) I'm sort of split on the propagation. First, it defeats the purpose of not being overpowered when it can basically duplicate itself hundreds of time, and it also makes it hard for The Foundation to find all of those needles. On the other hand, it makes it into a potential plague and that's sort of an interesting concept.</p>
<p>All I can suggest here is that you may want to put a duration on the longevity of the duplicated needles of maybe a week.</p>
<p>2) Also, just to make things interesting from a dramatic perspective, a duration on how long the effect can last would be interesting as well (there's just something I like about a woman giving her staff the whatfor and then realizing she screwed up); otherwise it just feels like you're creating SCPs that will have a long duration, and are likely to be destroyed or at least retired once someone makes the connection.</p>
<p>3) I think people are bored with SCPs that only do negative things in a negative way. It would be interesting if it magnified ANY emotion that the seamstress had while using it. Also, point out that people prick their thumbs a lot while sewing, especially while emotionally distracted; that's they invented thimbles!</p>
<p>The combo of expanding its ability and pointing out how often it happens ups it threat level a little, and in potentially interesting ways.</p>
<p>Otherwise, a good start!</p>

							</div>

								
					
